<title>BURKINA FASO: SOCCER-BURKINA FASO NAMES AFRICA NATIONS CUP MASCOT.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BURKINA FASO NAMES AFRICA NATIONS CUP MASCOT.</headline>
<dateline>OUAGADOUGOU 1997-02-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Burkina Faso, host of the 1998 African Nations Cup finals, has named the mascot for the competition Fofo -- which means &quot;welcome&quot; in the langage of its semi-nomadic Fulani minority.</p>
<p>A jury composed of men of letters, journalists and representatives of society at large selected the name, which is also understood by Fulani across West Africa, from 109 suggestions, organising committee officials said on Friday.</p>
<p>The mascot, a football with a smiling face, a traditional Sapone hat, football socks and outstretched arms, had been waiting for a name since it was first presented to the public on December 27.</p>
<p>The Sapone hat, a little like a Chinese coolie hat, is widely worn by the West African nation's Mossi majority. It too is a symbol of welcome.</p>
<p>The last Nations Cup finals were held in South Africa in 1996.</p>
</text>
